Give the scripts sfall's virtual files

CE had fs_copy, fs_find and fs_delete only, as path aliases: a script could
not change what it copied. The Restoration Project copies critters' art and
rewrites its frame rate (gl_k_walking_speed, gl_k_goris_derobing) with
fs_seek, fs_read_short and fs_write_short.

The files now hold their bytes, as in sfall: fs_create, fs_copy, the reads and
writes of bytes, shorts, ints, floats and strings (high byte first), fs_size,
fs_pos, fs_seek and fs_resize. The engine reads a virtual file wherever it
opens the game file of its name (sound effects aside, as before), through a
read-only stream of a copy of its bytes. Files a script asks to keep
(fs_resize(id, -1)) go in sfallfs.sav, in sfall's layout; a slot saved with
none has none.
